XenServer Packer plugin — release signing key
=============================================

This file holds the OpenPGP public key that signs XenServer Packer plugin
releases. Each release carries a detached signature over its checksum file,
`packer-plugin-xenserver_v<version>_SHA256SUMS.sig`, made with this key.

The key travels with the releases it signs, so on its own it cannot establish
that a release is genuine: anyone able to replace the artifacts could replace
this file too. What it does give you is a check on a corrupted or truncated
download, and -- once you have recorded the fingerprint below -- a way to
notice if the signing key ever changes. Record it the first time you verify a
release. See "Verifying a release" in README.md.

